# flip-focus (H5): b's toggle focused by Tab — reached deterministically by
# clicking b's box (331, 555: its centre at 1440x900, focuses without changing
# the value) and Shift+Tab once back to its toggle (counting 7-8 Tabs from the
# body proved flaky: the first Tab is swallowed when the document has no
# focus). Expect the 3 px primary-32% ring, no outline. Behaviour: the DOM's
# activeElement is b's toggle ("Mirror left to right").
# flip-focus (H5): b's toggle focused by Tab — reached by clicking k's box
# (331, 494: its centre at 1440x900, focuses without changing the value) and
# a single forward Tab to the next stop, b's toggle. (Shift+Tab back from b's
# box overshoots to k's box in the harness's Python-driver WebKit while plain
# Tab advances exactly one stop; counting Tabs from the body is flaky because
# the first Tab is swallowed when the document has no focus. Both measured.)
# Expect the 3 px primary-32% ring, no outline. Behaviour: the DOM's
# activeElement is b's toggle ("Mirror left to right").
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
query a=2
wait 2000
click 331 494
wait 200
key Tab
wait 200
shot flip-focus
